cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "KAN-DI: Discriminative Bayesian Optimization with a Kolmogorov-Arnold Prior"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jaehyeong
    family-names: Choi
    affiliation: "Korea Institute of Science and Technology"
  - given-names: Kyeongsu
    family-names: Kim
    affiliation: "Korea Institute of Science and Technology"
  - given-names: Ung
    family-names: Lee
    affiliation: "Korea Institute of Science and Technology"
abstract: >-
  Bayesian optimization that uses a pruned Kolmogorov-Arnold network as the
  Gaussian-process prior mean and a composite acquisition function
  (exploitation, discrimination, uniformity) so that one optimization loop
  maximizes the response and identifies its governing descriptors at the
  same time. Descriptor importance is the average gradient energy (AGE),
  the squared partial derivative of the closed-form KAN response averaged
  over the candidate pool.
